# Shell scripts must stay LF in the working tree. This repo is developed on
# Windows (core.autocrlf=true), and a CRLF shell script breaks bash on Linux:
# the shebang line and `set -o pipefail` both fail on the stray CR. CI runs
# the host-side test script with bash, local dev runs it from WSL, and it
# affects e.g. tools/publish_ota.sh from a Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
